#: src/introduction.md:32
msgid "A note on output"
msgstr "Poznámka k výstupu"

#: src/introduction.md:34
msgid ""
"goat is built to be both a pleasure to use _and_ safe to script. Friendly "
"touches — a 🐐 when everything's green, a hint about your next step — only "
"ever appear on an interactive terminal. Pipe goat into a script or ask for "
"`--json` and you get clean, stable, machine-readable output with nothing "
"decorative in the way. Set `GOAT_NO_FUN=1` and even the interactive "
"flourishes go quiet."
msgstr ""
"goat je postavený tak, aby sa s ním dalo príjemne pracovať _a zároveň_ "
"bezpečne skriptovať. Priateľské detaily — 🐐, keď je všetko zelené, nápoveda "
"k vášmu ďalšiemu kroku — sa objavujú len v interaktívnom termináli. "
"Presmerujte goat do skriptu alebo si vyžiadajte `--json` a dostanete čistý, "
"stabilný, strojovo čitateľný výstup bez akýchkoľvek dekoratívnych prvkov. "
"Nastavte `GOAT_NO_FUN=1` a stíchnu aj interaktívne ozdoby."

#: src/getting-started.md:3
msgid ""
"You don't need a profile, a bundle, or a network to start. goat ships with a "
"sandbox so you can learn by doing, safely."
msgstr ""
"Na začiatok nepotrebujete profil, bundle ani sieť. goat sa dodáva so "
"sandboxom, takže sa môžete učiť praxou, bezpečne."

#: src/getting-started.md:5
msgid "1. Say hello"
msgstr "1. Pozdravte sa"

#: src/getting-started.md:11
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"◇ SANDBOX — simulated fabric, no real mesh. Run `goat init` to attach a real "
"env.\n"
"goat hello — saying `lo` to the fabric as `default` on topic `hello/"
"default`\n"
"  [t+  42ms] portal     accepted topic `hello/default` (simulated)\n"
"  [t+  74ms] fabric     routed `lo` to `hello/default` over the WireGuard "
"P2P path (simulated)\n"
"  [t+ 101ms] subscriber your subscriber received `lo` — round-trip complete "
"(simulated)\n"
"  └─ `lo`: the first message ever sent over a network (ARPANET, 29 Oct 1969) "
"— they typed \"LOGIN\" and the link crashed after two letters.\n"
"round-trip complete.\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"◇ SANDBOX — simulovaná fabric, žiadny skutočný mesh. Spustite `goat init`, "
"ak chcete pripojiť skutočné prostredie.\n"
"goat hello — hovorím `lo` fabric ako `default` na téme `hello/default`\n"
"  [t+  42ms] portal     prijal tému `hello/default` (simulované)\n"
"  [t+  74ms] fabric     smeroval `lo` na `hello/default` cez cestu WireGuard "
"P2P (simulované)\n"
"  [t+ 101ms] subscriber váš odberateľ prijal `lo` — spiatočná cesta "
"dokončená (simulované)\n"
"  └─ `lo`: prvá správa, aká bola kedy odoslaná po sieti (ARPANET, 29. okt. "
"1969) — napísali „LOGIN“ a spoj spadol po dvoch písmenách.\n"
"spiatočná cesta dokončená.\n"
"```"

#: src/getting-started.md:21
msgid ""
"`goat hello` publishes a message, subscribes to it, and watches it come back "
"— narrating every hop the data took. In the sandbox those hops are "
"simulated; against a real env they're real. Either way, when it says _round-"
"trip complete_, you know the path works end to end."
msgstr ""
"`goat hello` publikuje správu, prihlási sa k jej odberu a sleduje, ako sa "
"vráti — pričom rozpráva o každom skoku, ktorý dáta absolvovali. V sandboxe "
"sú tieto skoky simulované; voči skutočnému prostrediu sú skutočné. Či tak "
"alebo onak, keď sa zobrazí _spiatočná cesta dokončená_, viete, že cesta "
"funguje od začiatku do konca."

#: src/getting-started.md:23
msgid ""
"The message is `lo` on purpose — the first thing ever sent over a network."
msgstr "Správa je `lo` zámerne — prvá vec, aká bola kedy odoslaná po sieti."

#: src/getting-started.md:25
msgid "2. Take the tour"
msgstr "2. Absolvujte prehliadku"

#: src/getting-started.md:31
msgid ""
"`goat tutor` is a self-paced, hands-on tour — think `vimtutor` for the "
"fabric. Eight short lessons take you from \"what is this\" to publishing, "
"subscribing, diagnosing, and reading the substrate cascade. It runs in the "
"sandbox by default, saves your place, and you can stop and resume any time:"
msgstr ""
"`goat tutor` je praktická prehliadka vlastným tempom — predstavte si "
"`vimtutor` pre fabric. Osem krátkych lekcií vás prevedie od „čo to je“ až po "
"publikovanie, odoberanie, diagnostiku a čítanie kaskády substrátu. "
"Štandardne beží v sandboxe, ukladá vašu pozíciu a kedykoľvek môžete prestať "
"a pokračovať:"

#: src/getting-started.md:39
msgid "3. Attach a real environment"
msgstr "3. Pripojte skutočné prostredie"

#: src/getting-started.md:41
msgid ""
"When you've been issued an onboarding **bundle** (a `.cbor` file with your "
"identity), the wizard takes it from here:"
msgstr ""
"Keď vám bol vydaný onboardingový **bundle** (súbor `.cbor` s vašou "
"identitou), sprievodca prevezme zvyšok:"

#: src/getting-started.md:49
msgid ""
"`goat init` is the friendly front door — it detects whether you're set up, "
"lets you choose the sandbox or a real env, proves it works, and points you "
"at the tutor. `goat doctor` then runs a stepped reachability check (mesh → "
"router → certificate → portal) and, if anything's wrong, tells you exactly "
"what to fix."
msgstr ""
"`goat init` je priateľské vstupné dvere — zistí, či ste nastavení, umožní "
"vám vybrať sandbox alebo skutočné prostredie, dokáže, že to funguje, a "
"nasmeruje vás na tutor. `goat doctor` potom spustí postupnú kontrolu "
"dosiahnuteľnosti (mesh → router → certifikát → portál) a ak je niečo zle, "
"presne vám povie, čo opraviť."

#: src/getting-started.md:51
msgid ""
"When all of doctor's steps pass, you'll see a small 🐐 — you're on the "
"fabric."
msgstr "Keď prejdú všetky kroky doctora, uvidíte malú 🐐 — ste na fabric."

#: src/getting-started.md:53
msgid "Where to next"
msgstr "Kam ďalej"

#: src/getting-started.md:55
msgid "New to the ideas? Read **[How the fabric works](concepts.md)**."
msgstr ""
"Tieto myšlienky sú pre vás nové? Prečítajte si **[Ako funguje fabric]"
"(concepts.md)**."

#: src/getting-started.md:56
msgid "Ready to do things? Jump to **[Everyday tasks](everyday.md)**."
msgstr ""
"Pripravení niečo robiť? Prejdite na **[Každodenné úlohy](everyday.md)**."

#: src/getting-started.md:57
msgid "Something not working? **[Troubleshooting](troubleshooting.md)**."
msgstr "Niečo nefunguje? **[Riešenie problémov](troubleshooting.md)**."

#: src/concepts.md:3
msgid ""
"You can use goat productively with just three ideas: **identity**, "
"**topics**, and **no broker**. Here they are."
msgstr ""
"goat môžete produktívne používať len s tromi myšlienkami: **identita**, "
"**témy** a **žiadny broker**. Tu sú."

#: src/concepts.md:5
msgid "A mesh you join with an identity"
msgstr "Mesh, do ktorého sa pripájate s identitou"

#: src/concepts.md:7
msgid ""
"The fabric is a self-healing mesh. Peers connect **directly** to each other "
"over encrypted WireGuard tunnels — once you're enrolled, your data doesn't "
"route through a central server, and your connections survive a management-"
"plane outage or a flaky uplink."
msgstr ""
"Fabric je samoopravujúci sa mesh. Uzly sa pripájajú **priamo** k sebe cez "
"šifrované tunely WireGuard — keď ste raz zaregistrovaní, vaše dáta sa "
"nesmerujú cez centrálny server a vaše spojenia prežijú výpadok riadiacej "
"roviny alebo nestabilné pripojenie."

#: src/concepts.md:9
msgid ""
"You join with an **identity**: an onboarding _bundle_ that carries your "
"certificate, an access token, and where the fabric lives. The fabric admits "
"you by _who you are_, not by a shared password. `goat profile init "
"<bundle.cbor>` installs that identity; you can hold several under different "
"_contexts_ and switch between them."
msgstr ""
"Pripájate sa s **identitou**: onboardingovým _bundlom_, ktorý nesie váš "
"certifikát, prístupový token a údaj, kde fabric žije. Fabric vás vpustí "
"podľa toho, _kto ste_, nie podľa zdieľaného hesla. `goat profile init "
"<bundle.cbor>` túto identitu nainštaluje; môžete mať viacero identít pod "
"rôznymi _kontextami_ a prepínať medzi nimi."

#: src/concepts.md:19
msgid "Topics: publish and subscribe"
msgstr "Témy: publikovanie a odoberanie"

#: src/concepts.md:21
msgid ""
"Data moves on **topics** — slash-delimited paths like `acme/radar1/tracks`. "
"The model is publish/subscribe:"
msgstr ""
"Dáta sa pohybujú po **témach** — cestách oddelených lomítkami ako `acme/"
"radar1/tracks`. Model je publish/subscribe:"

#: src/concepts.md:23
msgid "**Publish** (`goat pub <topic> <payload>`) writes a value to a topic."
msgstr "**Publish** (`goat pub <topic> <payload>`) zapíše hodnotu do témy."

#: src/concepts.md:24
msgid ""
"**Subscribe** (`goat sub <topic>`) receives every value published there, "
"live, as long as you're allowed to read it."
msgstr ""
"**Subscribe** (`goat sub <topic>`) prijíma každú tam publikovanú hodnotu, "
"naživo, pokiaľ ju smiete čítať."

#: src/concepts.md:26
msgid ""
"A topic is just a name; you create it (`goat topic create`), publish to it, "
"and anyone permitted can subscribe. `goat hello` is simply a publish and a "
"subscribe wired together so you can watch a value make the round trip."
msgstr ""
"Téma je len názov; vytvoríte ju (`goat topic create`), publikujete do nej a "
"každý oprávnený sa môže prihlásiť k jej odberu. `goat hello` je jednoducho "
"publikovanie a odoberanie prepojené dohromady, aby ste mohli sledovať, ako "
"hodnota absolvuje spiatočnú cestu."

#: src/concepts.md:28
msgid "No broker — and why that matters"
msgstr "Žiadny broker — a prečo na tom záleží"

#: src/concepts.md:30
msgid ""
"There is **no central broker** sitting in the middle of the data path. When "
"you publish, the value flows over the mesh directly to the peers subscribed "
"to it. That's deliberate: it removes the single bottleneck and single point "
"of failure that a broker would be."
msgstr ""
"Uprostred dátovej cesty nesedí **žiadny centrálny broker**. Keď publikujete, "
"hodnota tečie cez mesh priamo k uzlom, ktoré sú k nej prihlásené. Je to "
"zámer: odstraňuje to jediné úzke hrdlo a jediný bod zlyhania, ktorým by "
"broker bol."

#: src/concepts.md:32
msgid ""
"A practical consequence: **reads are broad, writes are the cut.** Being able "
"to _read_ a topic is permissive by design; _writing_ to one is governed by "
"your identity. So you'll rarely be surprised by what you can subscribe to, "
"and the integrity of what's published is anchored to who published it."
msgstr ""
"Praktický dôsledok: **čítanie je široké, zápis je rez.** Schopnosť _čítať_ "
"tému je z princípu povoľná; _zápis_ do nej riadi vaša identita. Takže vás "
"málokedy prekvapí to, k čomu sa môžete prihlásiť, a integrita publikovaného "
"je ukotvená v tom, kto to publikoval."

#: src/concepts.md:34
msgid "Sandbox vs. real"
msgstr "Sandbox vs. skutočné"

#: src/concepts.md:36
msgid ""
"Everything above has a faithful **in-process simulation** — the sandbox. "
"`goat hello --sandbox`, `goat init --sandbox`, and `goat tutor` exercise the "
"same shapes (a topic, a publish, a round-trip, a verdict) with no network "
"and no identity, so you can learn the model before you touch the real "
"fabric. The sandbox always says so with a `◇ SANDBOX` banner, and it never "
"writes to or reads from a real mesh."
msgstr ""
"Všetko vyššie má vernú **simuláciu v rámci procesu** — sandbox. `goat hello "
"--sandbox`, `goat init --sandbox` a `goat tutor` precvičujú rovnaké tvary "
"(téma, publikovanie, spiatočná cesta, verdikt) bez siete a bez identity, "
"takže sa môžete naučiť model ešte predtým, než sa dotknete skutočnej fabric. "
"Sandbox to vždy oznámi bannerom `◇ SANDBOX` a nikdy nezapisuje do skutočného "
"meshu ani z neho nečíta."

#: src/concepts.md:38
msgid ""
"When you switch to a real env, the _commands don't change_ — only the "
"backing does."
msgstr ""
"Keď prepnete na skutočné prostredie, _príkazy sa nemenia_ — mení sa len to, "
"čo je za nimi."

#: src/concepts.md:40
msgid ""
"Want the deeper architecture (the relay fallback, the access model, the "
"audit trail)? Ask your goat administrator for the design references — this "
"guide stays focused on operating the CLI."
msgstr ""
"Chcete hlbšiu architektúru (záložný relay, model prístupu, audit trail)? "
"Požiadajte svojho administrátora goat o návrhové referencie — táto príručka "
"sa zameriava na prevádzku CLI."

#: src/everyday.md:3
msgid ""
"The commands you'll actually reach for, as quick recipes. Add `--help` to "
"any of them for the full set of flags, or see the **[Command reference]"
"(reference.md)**."
msgstr ""
"Príkazy, po ktorých skutočne siahnete, ako rýchle recepty. Pridajte ku "
"ktorémukoľvek z nich `--help` pre úplnú sadu prepínačov, alebo si pozrite "
"**[Referenciu príkazov](reference.md)**."

#: src/everyday.md:5
msgid "Check you're connected"
msgstr "Skontrolujte, či ste pripojení"

#: src/everyday.md:12
msgid ""
"`goat doctor` is your first stop whenever something feels off — each step "
"that fails prints a specific remediation. When everything's green, both "
"commands give you a clear all-clear."
msgstr ""
"`goat doctor` je vaša prvá zastávka vždy, keď sa niečo zdá byť v nepríjemnom "
"stave — každý krok, ktorý zlyhá, vypíše konkrétnu nápravu. Keď je všetko "
"zelené, oba príkazy vám dajú jasné „všetko v poriadku“."

#: src/everyday.md:14
msgid "Publish and subscribe"
msgstr "Publikovanie a odoberanie"

#: src/everyday.md:16
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat sub 'acme/radar1/tracks'             # watch a topic live (Ctrl-C to "
"stop)\n"
"goat sub 'acme/**'                        # a whole subtree\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}'     # publish a payload\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat sub 'acme/radar1/tracks'             # sledovať tému naživo (Ctrl-C na "
"zastavenie)\n"
"goat sub 'acme/**'                        # celý podstrom\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}'     # publikovať payload\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:22
msgid "Want to see the ripple a publish sets off? Add `--narrate`:"
msgstr ""
"Chcete vidieť vlnenie, ktoré publikovanie vyvolá? Pridajte `--narrate`:"

#: src/everyday.md:24
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}' --narrate\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat pub acme/radar1/tracks '{\"t\":1}' --narrate\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:28
msgid "Work with topics"
msgstr "Práca s témami"

#: src/everyday.md:30
msgid ""
"```text\n"
"goat topic ls                              # list topics\n"
"goat topic ls acme                         # drill into an org/prefix\n"
"goat topic show acme/radar1/tracks         # one topic's full record\n"
"goat topic create acme/radar1/tracks --format protobuf:Track --description "
"\"live tracks\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```text\n"
"goat topic ls                              # vypísať témy\n"
"goat topic ls acme                         # vnoriť sa do organizácie/"
"prefixu\n"
"goat topic show acme/radar1/tracks         # úplný záznam jednej témy\n"
"goat topic create acme/radar1/tracks --format protobuf:Track --description "
"\"live tracks\"\n"
"```"

#: src/everyday.md:37
msgid ""
"After you create a topic, goat nudges you toward the natural next step "
"(watch it, or publish to it)."
msgstr ""
"Po vytvorení témy vás goat nasmeruje na prirodzený ďalší krok (sledovať ju "
"alebo do nej publikovať)."

#: src/everyday.md:39
msgid "Diagnose a problem"
msgstr "Diagnostikovať problém"

#: src/everyday.md:47
msgid ""
"`inspect` returns findings and the remedy for each — what's wrong and what "
"to do about it."
msgstr ""
"`inspect` vráti zistenia a nápravu pre každé z nich — čo je zle a čo s tým "
"robiť."

#: src/everyday.md:49
msgid "Scripting"
msgstr "Skriptovanie"

#: src/everyday.md:51
msgid ""
"Every command that prints a human view also offers `--json` for a stable, "
"machine-readable one. The JSON form never carries banners, hints, or "
"flourishes, and its shape and your exit code stay constant across releases "
"and languages:"
msgstr ""
"Každý príkaz, ktorý vypíše ľudský pohľad, ponúka aj `--json` pre stabilný, "
"strojovo čitateľný pohľad. Forma JSON nikdy nenesie bannery, nápovedy ani "
"ozdoby a jej tvar i váš návratový kód zostávajú nemenné naprieč vydaniami a "
"jazykmi:"

#: src/everyday.md:58
msgid "This is the contract: **friendly on a terminal, clean in a pipe.**"
msgstr "Toto je zmluva: **priateľský v termináli, čistý v rúre.**"

#: src/everyday.md:60
msgid ""
"One caution: `goat status` opens a real session at the router each time it runs, so it is a check you run when you want an answer, not something to poll from a timer. For a trend over time use `goat health` or `goat top`, which read what the goatnet already publishes."
msgstr ""
"Jedno upozornenie: `goat status` pri každom spustení otvorí skutočnú reláciu k routeru, takže je to kontrola, ktorú spúšťate, keď chcete odpoveď, nie niečo, čo sa má volať z časovača. Pre trend v čase použite `goat health` alebo `goat top`, ktoré čítajú to, čo goatnet už publikuje."

#: src/install.md:3
msgid ""
"goat is a single self-contained binary — no runtime, no dependencies. It's "
"served mesh-internally from `get.<your-goatnet>` (you're already on the mesh "
"if you can read this), and the version here always matches the binary that "
"surface serves."
msgstr ""
"goat je jediná samostatná binárka — žiadny runtime, žiadne závislosti. "
"Servuje sa interne v meshi z `get.<your-goatnet>` (ak toto čítate, už ste v "
"meshi) a verzia tu vždy zodpovedá binárke, ktorú daný povrch servuje."

#: src/install.md:5
msgid "Quick install"
msgstr "Rýchla inštalácia"

#: src/install.md:7
msgid "**macOS / Linux**"
msgstr "**macOS / Linux**"

#: src/install.md:10
msgid ""
"$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')              # darwin | linux\n"
msgstr ""
"$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')              # darwin | linux\n"

#: src/install.md:11
msgid "$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')  # amd64 | arm64\n"
msgstr ""
"$(uname -m | sed 's/x86_64/amd64/;s/aarch64/arm64/')  # amd64 | arm64\n"

#: src/install.md:12
msgid "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""
msgstr "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""

#: src/install.md:17
msgid "Make sure `~/.local/bin` is on your `PATH`."
msgstr "Uistite sa, že `~/.local/bin` je vo vašom `PATH`."

#: src/install.md:19
msgid "**Windows (PowerShell)**"
msgstr "**Windows (PowerShell)**"

#: src/install.md:21
msgid ""
"```powershell\n"
"iwr \"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-windows-amd64.exe\" -OutFile "
"\"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\"\n"
"& \"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\" --version\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
"```powershell\n"
"iwr \"https://get.<your-goatnet>/goat-windows-amd64.exe\" -OutFile "
"\"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\"\n"
"& \"$env:USERPROFILE\\goat.exe\" --version\n"
"```"

#: src/install.md:26
msgid ""
"Every subcommand works on Windows except `goat client` (the local tunnel "
"daemon), which is Linux/macOS-only."
msgstr ""
"Každý podpríkaz funguje na Windowse okrem `goat client` (lokálneho "
"tunelového démona), ktorý je len pre Linux/macOS."

#: src/install.md:28
msgid "Verify the download (recommended)"
msgstr "Overte sťahovanie (odporúčané)"

#: src/install.md:30
msgid ""
"The download surface publishes a per-binary `*.sha256` and an aggregate "
"`SHA256SUMS`. For a high-assurance install, verify before you run:"
msgstr ""
"Sťahovací povrch publikuje pre každú binárku `*.sha256` a súhrnný "
"`SHA256SUMS`. Pre inštaláciu s vysokou istotou overte ešte pred spustením:"

#: src/install.md:33
msgid "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>\""
msgstr "\"https://get.<your-goatnet>\""

#: src/install.md:34
msgid "\"$BASE/SHA256SUMS\""
msgstr "\"$BASE/SHA256SUMS\""

#: src/install.md:35
msgid "\"$BASE/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""
msgstr "\"$BASE/goat-${OS}-${ARCH}\""

#: src/install.md:35
msgid "# macOS: shasum -a 256 -c   ·   Linux: sha256sum -c\n"
msgstr "# macOS: shasum -a 256 -c   ·   Linux: sha256sum -c\n"

#: src/install.md:41
msgid "Platforms"
msgstr "Platformy"

#: src/install.md:43
msgid "OS"
msgstr "OS"

#: src/install.md:43
msgid "Architectures"
msgstr "Architektúry"

